{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem of placing two indistinguishable pieces on an \\(8 \\times 8\\) chessboard such that the pieces are either in the same row or the same column, we can break the problem into two parts: placing the pieces in the same row and placing the pieces in the same column.\n\n### Step 1: Placing the pieces in the same row\nThere are 8 rows on the chessboard. For each row, we can choose 2 out of the 8 columns to place the pieces. The number of ways to choose 2 columns out of 8 is given by the combination formula \\(\\binom{8}{2}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{2} = \\frac{8!}{2!(8-2)!} = \\frac{8 \\times 7}{2 \\times 1} = 28\n\\]\n\nSince there are 8 rows, the total number of ways to place the pieces in the same row is:\n\n","prefix_end":708,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,315,24047,1378,1257,88647,480,9666,389,458,17767,23,1124,15136,220,23,57758,32719,2482,1741,429,279,9666,525,2987,304,279,1852,2802,476,279,1852,3250,11,582,646,1438,279,3491,1119,1378,5479,25,24047,279,9666,304,279,1852,2802,323,24047,279,9666,304,279,1852,3250,382,14374,14822,220,16,25,1818,4527,279,9666,304,279,1852,2802,198,3862,525,220,23,6978,389,279,32719,2482,13,1752,1817,2802,11,582,646,5157,220,17,700,315,279,220,23,8147,311,1992,279,9666,13,576,1372,315,5510,311,5157,220,17,8147,700,315,220,23,374,2661,553,279,10601,14806,1124,11520,6863,316,90,23,15170,17,11035,3593,59,9640,59,6863,316,90,23,15170,17,92,284,1124,37018,90,23,0,15170,17,10297,23,12,17,41295,92,284,1124,37018,90,23,1124,15136,220,22,15170,17,1124,15136,220,16,92,284,220,17,23,198,59,2533,12549,1052,525,220,23,6978,11,279,2790,1372,315,5510,311,1992,279,9666,304,279,1852,2802,374,1447,59,9640,23,1124,15136,220,17,23,284,220,17,17,19,198,59,2533,14374,14822,220,17,25,1818,4527,279,9666,304,279,1852,3250,198,67691,11,1052,525,220,23,8147,389,279,327